{"schema_version":2,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"rao:4-21","provision":"RAO 4-21","book":"rao","book_name":"Rules of Assembly Operations","abbreviation":"RAO","reference":"4-21","title":"Section 4-21 of Article 4","supplementary":true,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/rao/4-21/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#rao/4-21","current_text":{"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Committees and commissions of the General Assembly established by the Book of Church Order and these Rules, except the Overtures Committee and Committees of Commissioners, may meet electronically (see RONR [12th ed.] 9:30-36) if that committee or commission so determines according to its own rules. Ad hoc and ad interim committees and commissions are authorized to meet electronically at the call of the Chairman or Convenor.</p>","text":"Committees and commissions of the General Assembly established by the Book of Church Order and these Rules, except the Overtures Committee and Committees of Commissioners, may meet electronically (see RONR [12th ed.] 9:30-36) if that committee or commission so determines according to its own rules. Ad hoc and ad interim committees and commissions are authorized to meet electronically at the call of the Chairman or Convenor."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"94a0b54eec213ad53deb08f9fe4e387f46d90e3373f4cd38647b018d7b192c88","parent_id":null,"children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recomme